WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.868
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Tina Fey.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.267
You sent me a very lovely text

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:07.033
that was both complimentary
and maybe a little concerned

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:09.300
after you saw "Day Drinking
with Seth and Lizzo."

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.467
-Yes.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:13.400
I watched it, we all did,
and it was hilarious

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.501
and fantastic, and Lizzo
is the best, obviously.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.968
But I texted you and Shoemaker
and said, like,

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:21.467
"But you don't really
drink all that, right?"

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.601
And Shoemaker wrote back,
"He does drink all of that,

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:26.400
and he actually drinks
more than that

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.534
and we have to cut it down
for air,

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:31.534
because the network is worried
it's irresponsible."

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:33.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:36.667
And so then I went back
and I re-watched, like,

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:39.434
Ina Garten,
and I became concerned for you.

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:41.501
-Yeah.
-That's so much alcohol.

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:42.567
-I know, it's...

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:44.601
And I'm not getting any younger.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:48.000
I really wear it for, like,
a full week.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.534
-I was gonna say, 'cause
I wanted to say to you,

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:54.067
"Can I do an imitation of
what I imagine

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:55.868
your lovely spouse, Alexi,
must feel like

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:57.400
when you come home from
one of those?"

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.634
-I'll tell you how
accurate it is.

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.767
-Okay, 'cause I feel like,
if I were your wife

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:02.734
and you came home from
day drinking with Lizzo,

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:03.834
I would be like this.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:06.734
I'd be like, "It was good?

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:08.901
Okay. No, th--

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.534
No, we don't want to
go out for subs."

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:13.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.934
"No, the kids ate.

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:17.167
Okay.

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.133
Wow."

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:22.033
"Either brush your teeth
or go to bed."

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:24.767
Is it that kind of a...?

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.801
-And I will tell you that
two back,

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:29.701
she said, "I have an idea.

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.601
I think you, when it's over,

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:33.601
I think you should stay
at a nearby hotel."

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:34.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:36.734
-I actually sort of assumed
that maybe you did.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:39.167
-She was like, "Why don't you
let yourself off the hook

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:40.267
for a night?"
-Yeah.

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.234
Instead of coming back
and being like,

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.334
"Oh, she was so funny?
Great."

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.067
-Yeah, yeah.
She loves hearing --

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:46.400
She loves me being really drunk,
sort of like just

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.501
singing the praises
of a pop star.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:49.501
-Oh, of Rihanna, yeah.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:52.200
-"Rihanna's so real!"

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.834
-I bet. She's so real.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:55.334
-She's so happy.
That was her happiest day.

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:57.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.601 --> 00:02:00.300
When we were texting,
when you wrote me that,

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.534
I was like, "Where are you?"

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.434
And you were in London,
working on a movie

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:04.601
with Kenneth Branagh.

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:05.467
-Yes!
-That's amazing.

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:06.901
-It's crazy, right?

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:09.334
So yeah, I got to go to London
for three months

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.467
and work on this movie called
"A Haunting in Venice."

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:13.367
Which -- I'll come back
when it comes out.

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.667
I'll tell you about it then.
-Okay, okay.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:18.834
-But I loved getting a chance
to live in London

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.834
and come back, I'm insufferable.

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:22.567
I say things like
"jacket potato" now.

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:25.133
-Oh, wow. That's a good one.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:26.200
You've got to really be there
for like --

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.601
-"Do you have a jacket potato?"

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:29.234
What?

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:31.133
It's so nice there.

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:36.267
Oh, my gosh, the subway system
is like -- mm! -- stab-free.

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:39.100
-Oh, that's nice.
You don't miss it a little bit?

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.467
You don't miss the thrill
of like,

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:41.901
is today the day I get stabbed?

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:45.400
-Yeah, I don't miss the,
like, "Serpico" vibe, no.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.267
You can buy wine
in the grocery store.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.367
Also everything has
adorable names.

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:52.634
Every product has like,
everything's cute.

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:53.701
So you'll be like,

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:55.801
"Can I just get some
fizzy nobblers?

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:59.767
They're tampons, right?
The fizzy nobblers."

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:01.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:04.400
"And the gabbledy-gos?

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.567
The suppositories for when
you're constipated, yes."

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:09.567
Everything's just charming.

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:11.467
-Those are the gabbeldy-gos?
-Yeah, gabbeldy-gos.

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:12.801
-Oh, that's helpful to know.

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.467
-Yeah, if you get there,
you want to get gabbeldy-gorps,

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:15.501
'cause you've traveled.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:16.667
-'Cause you know how I am
when I fly.

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.133
-You don't.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:21.167
-I need them like, immediately.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.701
-But it was delightful,

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:26.501
and I'm sure you know from your
one night drunk in the hotel,

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:28.601
being away from your family

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:30.400
is wonderful.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:33.000
It's wonderful.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.701
-The only thing that's better
than me being in a hotel

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.100
a block away,

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.701
being away from your family
in a different timezone?

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:43.067
And you gotta be like,
"I tried to call.

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:44.667
You were asleep."
-Yes!

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:46.400
My husband would call me
and be like,

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.300
"Both dogs have diarrhea,"
and I'd be like,

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.834
"Oh, it's night time here.

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:53.601
I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry."

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:56.200
And then they got to come
to London for Christmas,

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.501
which was great.
-Perfect.

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:59.367
-And we all had
a wonderful time,

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.767
but I felt like a person
who had

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:06.367
escaped a cult and then was
pulled back into that cult.

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:08.200
-That scene where the cult
find you.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.400
-Yes, where like, the weird guy
in shorts comes to you and says,

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.868
"Hey, you've really forgotten
your belief system.

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:18.667
Remember, what we believe here
is that you gain value

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:21.133
in your life by picking up
our wet towels."

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:22.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:24.701
"This is who you are.

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:26.567
Look, look how many shoes
we brought."

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:27.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:31.634
-We're very happy
you went back.

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:33.801
-And I was like, "You're right,
you guys are probably right."

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:35.167
And then I came home.

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:36.267
-Well, we're very happy
to have you back in the city.

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:38.567
-Thank you.
-Last thing before you go,

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:41.234
there's gonna be a new season
of "Girls5eva" on Netflix,

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:42.567
which is really exciting.
-Yes! Very excited.

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:45.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.767
Yes.

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:49.701
Seasons 1 and 2 are still
available on Peacock,

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:50.934
our friends at Peacock
have those.

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:54.067
If you are a jacket potato
in the UK,

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:55.901
you can see 1 and 2 on Netflix.
-That's great.

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:57.033
-Elsewhere in the world.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.300
And then Season 3's gonna be
on Netflix.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.434
We're starting shooting soon.
I'm super excited.

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:03.100
Meredith Scardino is the
funniest person in the world.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:07.133
And of course, Paula Pell,
Sara Bareilles, Rene Goldsberry,

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:08.701
Busy Phillips.

00:05:08.701 --> 00:05:09.901
-That's great.
It's a great cast.

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:11.400
It's a great show.
So happy to have you here.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.934
Congratulations on the tour!
-Thank you guys!

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:14.567
-Sold out! Tina Fey.

00:05:14.567 --> 00:05:17.367
For more information
on Restless Leg Tour,

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:18.834
go to TinaAmyTour.com

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:20.634
to find out it's too late
to get tickets.

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.801
We'll be right back
with Nate Bargatze.

